# Break-glass entries for scripts/ci/carry-previous-release.sh (#1607 note 48548).
#
# When a ref's previous release can no longer be carried (its artifacts expired,
# or its signing key was deleted), the next release fails. Add one line here,
# commit it and have it reviewed like any other change; the push is the recovery.
#
# Line format, fields split on spaces; blank lines and lines starting with # are
# ignored:
#
#   <ref> <record_image job id> <reason>
#
#   <ref>                 the branch being released (preview, hotfix/x.y)
#   <record_image job id> the id of the predecessor's record_image job, as the
#                         failed job's message names it
#   <reason>              the rest of the line; required, logged on acceptance
#
# Rule: --prepare honours a line only when the predecessor it found is that job
# on that ref, and the failure was a 404 on that build's manifest or signature or
# a signature that verifies against no trusted key. It then logs
# "gap accepted for record_image job N on <ref> (<reason>)" and treats the ref as
# a first release: nothing is carried. A line for another job or ref is logged as
# stale and ignored; a malformed line fails --prepare naming it. A line never
# excuses a carried previous/ pair or a tooling failure, nor an API error, an
# empty signature file or a missing sign_evidence job.
#
# Remove the line once the next release on the ref has landed.
